THIS IS THE FOURTH PASS IN A ROW TO FIND CELLS OF ONE SPACE.  The class-closure amendment already governed repair 2;
what repair 2's enumeration missed was not a cell of the handler's inputs but the INSTANCE every row is built on
(a calloc with seeded interrupt fields and one shared interrupt counter pair) and the PRODUCER's domains (the
widths the ARM load/store unit emits, the lines a device raises, the fields only the producer writes).

== THE SPACE, restated with the two axes repair 2 did not name ==
  handler inputs (unchanged): case label; writeflag; len; idata; irq_status, irq_enable, fiq_status, fiq_enable;
    the five latches.  The bodies test: direction; own latch; (irq_status & new enable) {0, nonzero} in the Clear
    write.
  PRODUCER domains: len is {1, 2, 4} everywhere and 8 at +0x180 and +0x280 only (LDRD/STRD align down to 8;
    cpu_arm_instr_loadstore.c) -- the Opus seat showed 8 at an unaligned site is not a guest input; irq_status is
    written only by footbridge_interrupt_assert(), for lines 4-7 (timers), 10 (cats ISA), 11 (netwinder ISA), 18
    (cats PCI); irq_asserted is written only there and in footbridge_interrupt_deassert().
  INSTANCE fields no branch of the five reads, on which an edit can still condition a test: irq_asserted, the timer
    fields (DEVINIT: PERIODIC, TIMER_MAX_VAL, bound 1; the rows' calloc: 0), pending_timer_interrupts.
  OUTPUT channel: WHICH interrupt a Clear write drives (d->irq, not a timer interrupt) -- every block before X14
    counts both on one pair.

